<title>UK: Savoy Hotel pretax, prexcep profit rises.</title>
<headline>Savoy Hotel pretax, prexcep profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 1996.</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)  A		 38.8	     vs     27.1</p>
<p> Shr (pence)  B		 19.4	     vs     13.5</p>
<p> Total Dividend (pence) A   17.5	     vs     14.0</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) B    8.7	     vs	7.0</p>
<p> Pretax			   15.2	     vs     11.3</p>
<p> Turnover			 91.4	     vs     89.0</p>
<p>NOTE - The pretax profit does not take exceptional expenses into account. The group said it had incurred exceptional costs of 39.9 million stg on a restoration programme for some of its hotels.</p>
<p>Full company name - Savoy Hotel Plc</p>
</text>
